The following represent problems that were discovered far too late in the
distribution process to correct fully.

/usr/src/lib/libc/com-sys5/Makefile

	Strtol.o was listed as strtol.c in the OBJS declaration.  The
	Makefile has been corrected on the tape, but the libraries
	/lib/libc.a and /usr/lib/libc_p.a don't have the strtol.o file in
	them.  Correct the problem by recompiling and reinstalling the
	library.

/usr/src/lib/libc/pdp/stdio/fgetc.s

	A trivial optimization was lost when our source disks crashed
	about a month and a half before we cut the distribution tape.
	Unfortunately we didn't catch it till too late.  Since we didn't
	like the idea of making a distribution where all the compiled
	binaries used a different version of fgetc than that in the
	delivered library, we offer the change here.  We ran with the
	optimization for about a month without any problems.  The change
	saves one word in fgetc and makes it run minorly faster.

	*** /usr/src/lib/libc/pdp/stdio/fgetc.s	Wed Feb 11 17:55:38 1987
	--- /tmp/fgetc.s	Sat Dec 31 00:13:58 1988
	***************
	*** 25,33 ****
	  	mov	2(sp),r1		/ grab iop
	  	dec	_CNT(r1)		/ any characters available?
	  	blt	1f
	! 	movb	*_PTR(r1),r0		/ grab the character,
	  	inc	_PTR(r1)		/ bop the pointer on one place,
	- 	bic	$!377,r0		/ and cast to u_char
	  	rts	pc
	  1:
	  	jmp	__filbuf		/ let _filbuf(iop) handle it
	--- 25,33 ----
	  	mov	2(sp),r1		/ grab iop
	  	dec	_CNT(r1)		/ any characters available?
	  	blt	1f
	! 	clr	r0			/ grab the character (unsigned),
	! 	bisb	*_PTR(r1),r0
	  	inc	_PTR(r1)		/ bop the pointer on one place,
	  	rts	pc
	  1:
	  	jmp	__filbuf		/ let _filbuf(iop) handle it


/usr/src/usr.bin/uucp/pk1.c

	Use of the select call to timeout incoming packets was disabled
	because the 2.10 select call wasn't performing correctly for
	some time.  Steven Schultz and Cyrus Rahman both state that
	uucico works properly now with the select code enabled (it also
	works without the code).

	The code is #ifndef'ed on "notdef" at line 384 of pk1.c and is
	commented as follows:

		/*
		 * XXX - 2.10BSD: This ifdef notdef should be removed as soon
		 * XXX - as select is properly implemented in 2.10BSD.  Casey.
		 */

	Uucico should operate better without this modification, but we
	didn't have time to tear it out and get it properly BETA tested.
	With Steven and Cyrus' reports, it's probably pretty safe to remove
	this modification ...
